# Vault production layout adapter

This owned isolated adapter proposes the exact frozen Vault draft/lifecycle runtime in its future app layout. Runtime `client.mjs`, `server.mjs`, `history.mjs`, `kdbx.mjs` and `xml.mjs` are byte-identical to the frozen 1454-artifact candidate. No production or shared files have been changed.

Only test path/output bindings change: the release executable uses the same production-relative locator/environment option as existing oracle tests and remains SHA-authenticated before every original process and assembly load; generated observations and synthetic workspace IDs move to ignored repo `.local/vault-history-fixtures/<pid>`; and the HTTP runner imports `../../server.mjs` to exercise the actual copied shared host with the real app layout. Test scenario bodies and native semantics are unchanged. The app README adds actual app-relative inert study/notice links. `adaptations.json` records each exact substitution and identity.

All 1454 frozen artifacts are preserved. The 1450 non-carrier artifacts are inert app-relative `.snapshot` files, including prior181/546 stages, original licenses/source, old receipts, four independent failed-review campaigns and complete raw runs. Four identical full source ZIP carrier copies remain local under `.local/stage-carriers`; no original executable is embedded. The preservation manifest binds each original path to its actual public/local disposition. Normal tests do not write `apps/results` and do not execute original code in application runtime.

The adapter separately replays the 41 candidate groups and the already independent review's 11 safety/control probes. The latter replay is author-run path adaptation, not a newly independent review. Original24 assembly loads, candidate DOM25 groups, repeated independent DOM11 probes, five genuine shared-host test processes and one additional private route host stay separate. Neither this adapter nor the original study executes the original dialog or Touch; no new browser check is claimed here. Historical compatibility18 is preserved without rebinding.

The recorder pins all runtime/test/helper/host/document inputs and all1454 retained artifacts before and after each collection. Child stdout/stderr caps and a90-second deadline do not imply hard fingerprint I/O deadlines, rollback of dispatched server operations or race-free Windows descendant cleanup. Source-assisted native history follows a bounded selected contract and retains upstream GPL-2.0-or-later source attribution. Full product parity, original-grade security and comparative superiority remain false.

The entire new independent review, including browser evidence, will be preserved separately after its reviewer-owned freeze; no mutable review inventory is relabeled as frozen here. Parent integration should install app proposals only and preserve the existing compatibility receipt and prior results; copied shared host/catalog/storage/public files are validation infrastructure, not proposed shared replacements.
